# Beril

Read `AGENTS.md` and `SKILL.md` before a security task.

If the target is in the sentence, run the matching command first. "Kır" or "açık bul" means scan, then one manual class. Behavior: `agents/front-desk.md`.

## Commands

```bash
./beril scan --target <url-or-path>
./beril recon --target <domain>
./beril scan --target <web> --profile smb
./beril secrets --target <dir> --history
./beril verify --new <host>
./beril scan --target <web> --active
./beril hunt --target <repo> --sandbox
./beril re --target <binary>
```

## Rules

- Confirm target and authorization first. No record, no active probe.
- Passive scan, then one manual class at a time.
- Static before dynamic. No execution of unknown binaries without a snapshot or sandbox.
- A scanner hit is a lead. Replay it.
- Mask secrets, revoke before history cleanup.
- Label confirmed and inferred. Keep evidence paths.
- Stop at the agreed proof.
